   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The substitution rule in indirect speech",
     "texto": [
      "When the Konjunktiv I form is identical to the present indicative (for example, in the plural: **sie haben, sie fordern, sie kommen**), standard German requires replacing it with **Konjunktiv II** (**sie hätten, sie forderten, sie kämen**) to clearly signal that these are other people's words.",
      "If the Konjunktiv II form in turn coincides with the indicative Präteritum (as in many weak verbs: **sie forderten**), or sounds archaic, the periphrasis with **würden + infinitive** (**sie würden fordern**) is usually used."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Original structure",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Substitute form (Konjunktiv II)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Periphrasis with «würden»",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
